surate with the successful applicant’s academic qualifications, current position and professional experience. The current maximum income tax rate in Macao is 12%, but is effectively around 5%–7% after various exemptions. Research Support CityU Macau provides one-off research start-up funding, research awards, conference funding, research and teaching assistants, equipment funding, and support for publication and language-editing fees. Faculty members in Macao are eligible to apply for both Macao research funds (e.g. the Science and Technology Development Fund and the Macao Foundation) and Mainland China research funds (e.g. the National Natural Science Foundation of China). Benefits CityU Macau offers paid annual, sick, marriage, maternity and paternity leave; medical, life, labour and travel insurance; retention bonus, housing allowance, meal allowance and a voluntary pension fund scheme. Staff also benefit from pre-service training, in-service study subsidies, the Young Scholars Exchange and Development Programme, and regular festive and staff activities. Application Procedures Applications must be submitted online; applications by email or post will not be accepted. Applicants should visit https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/category/job-application/teaching-en/ for more details and apply via https://career.cityu.edu.mo . Enquiries (not applications) may be sent to jobs@cityu.edu.mo. The position will remain open until filled. The following documents should be uploaded to the online application platform: Resume Personal Identification Document Graduation Certificates Cover Letter (clearly indicating the position, reference code and academic unit you are applying for) Contact information for three referees Review of applications will commence immediately. Applicants who are not invited for an interview within three months of submission should consider their applications unsuccessful. The successful candidate is expected to assume duty in December 2026 or mid-August 2027. 