    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/11/supervisor-senior-supervisor-institutional-research-and-analytics/": {
      "title": "Supervisor / Senior Supervisor(International Communications)",
      "description": "Supervisor / Senior Supervisor(International Communications) – Institutional Research and Analytics – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Supervisor / Senior Supervisor(International Communications) – Institutional Research and Analytics Job Description Assist in formulating the University’s publicity and promotion strategies to enhance its international academic and industry visibility; Write and produce content for the University’s international promotional platforms; Establish and maintain international scholars and industry partners database, with regular data updates, categorization, verification, and identification of potential collaboration opportunities; Coordinate and follow up on work related to the University’s international ranking and reputation surveys, providing operational guidelines, data templates, and progress tracking; Consolidate and analysis data regularly, and compile work reports; Support work process optimization and work efficiency enhancement; Perform other tasks and duties as assigned. Requirement Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Public Relations, Marketing, International Affairs, Education or related field; Master’s degree is preferred; Minimum of 5 years of related work experience; preferably in external communications, content strategy, public relations, social media management, international affairs, or higher education administration; Fluency in Cantonese, Mandarin, and English; proficiency in Chinese and English writing; Familiarity with international social media platforms in terms of content planning, daily management, and performance analysis; Strong cross-departmental coordination and project management skills; Proficient with Microsoft Office and AI tools to support daily work; Self-motivated, detail-oriented, with good communication and teamwork skills; Able to accommodate international time zones for liaison and willing to travel as required; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-11 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post Administrative Assistant Next post Supervisor / Senior Supervisor / Administrative Officer (Dormitory Management) – Facility Management Office Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/09/administrative-staff/": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant – 澳門城市大學人事處 Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Administrative Assistant Job Description Assist the department head in handling daily administrative matters, work schedules, and meeting arrangements; provide administrative and reception support; Assist in following up on full-cycle project management, as well as the drafting and production of reports and plans; Conduct thematic research and perform regular collection, consolidation, and management of data and information; Maintain close liaison and collaboration with internal and external departments/institutions; Perform other tasks and duties as assigned. Requirements Bachelor’s degree or above; Master’s degree is preferred; Minimum 3 years of relevant work experience; with work experience in Mainland China is preferred; Excellent Chinese writing skills and strong capacity for textual synthesis, with the ability to independently produce in-depth articles and reports; Optimistic and proactive, self-motivated with a strong sense of responsibility, well-organised, with a high level of confidentiality awareness, and the ability to multitask and work under pressure; and Fluency in Cantonese, Mandarin, and English; proficiency in Chinese writing; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-9 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post Project Executive / Project Coordinator Next post Supervisor / Senior Supervisor(International Communications) – Institutional Research and Analytics Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處"
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/09/project-executive-project-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Project Executive / Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Project Executive / Project Coordinator – 澳門城市大學人事處 Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Project Executive / Project Coordinator Job Description Coordinate and conduct thematic research on the University’s development strategies and major policy initiatives; Independently draft in-depth working papers and reports; Oversee full-cycle project management for major initiatives; Coordinate and maintain relationship networks with government entities, higher education institutions, external organisations, and industry chain partners; Perform other tasks and duties as assigned. Requirement Bachelor’s degree or above; Master’s degree is preferred; Minimum 5 years of relevant work experience; experience in copywriting or report drafting is preferred; Strong Chinese writing skills, with the ability to independently produce in-depth articles and reports; Possess keen awareness of current affairs, strategic thinking, innovative mindset, cross-cultural communication skills, and the ability to multitask and work under pressure; Self-motivated, well-organised, with a high sense of confidentiality, responsibility, and team spirit; Fluency in Cantonese, Mandarin, and English; proficiency in Chinese writing; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-9 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post Senior Supervisor / Administrative Officer – Facility Management Office Next post Administrative Assistant Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處"
