    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/08/senior-supervisor-administrative-officer-facility-management-office/": {
      "title": "Senior Supervisor / Administrative Officer",
      "description": "Senior Supervisor / Administrative Officer – Facility Management Office – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Senior Supervisor / Administrative Officer – Facility Management Office Job Description Lead the optimization and planning of the University’s Electrical and Mechanical (E&M) systems and projects; Oversee and coordinate the installation, operation, and maintenance of various E&M systems and equipment; Supervise and monitor the quality of maintenance services for E&M equipment across the University’s premises; Formulate and implement maintenance plans; Oversee the management of E&M drawings and ensure timely updates; Lead and coordinate the preparation of tender documentation for E&M system optimization projects; Coordinate and address unforeseen repair emergencies; Perform other tasks and duties as assigned. Requirement Bachelor’s degree or higher in Electrical and Mechanical (E&M) Engineering, Power Engineering, Mechanical Engineering or related disciplines; a Master’s degree is preferred; At least 4 years of relevant experience in large-scale E&M project management or facilities management; Proven experience in the design, installation, and supervision of power supply systems and air-conditioning systems; Proficiency in using AutoCAD for computer-aided design and drafting; Ability to read and interpret E&M engineering drawings; Fluent in Cantonese, Mandarin and English, with excellent Chinese and English writing skills; Detail-oriented with the ability to work independently; Experience in engineering tendering processes will be an advantage; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-8 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support , Job Application Post navigation Previous post Faculty Administrative Staff Next post Project Executive / Project Coordinator Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/08/faculty-administrative-staff-2/": {
      "title": "Faculty Administrative Staff",
      "description": "Faculty Administrative Staff – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Faculty Administrative Staff To cope with the development of the university, we are opening various new positions in different faculties. Job Description Responsible for the regular operation of the programs and daily administrative tasks of the faculty; Manage student records, student status changes, and coordinate affairs related to postgraduate thesis; Assist in coordinating faculty events and University-wide activities; Support administrative work related to Quality Assurance of the faculty’s programs; Handle inquiries and applications from teachers, students or other departments; Liaise and communicate with internal and external institutions, and to facilitate cooperation and exchanges with external universities; Handle general document processing and filing. Requirement Bachelor’s degree holder or above; Minimum 1 year of related work experience; candidates with more experience will be considered for higher position; Fluent in Cantonese, Mandarin and English, proficient in written Chinese and English; Familiar with the operation and systems of universities in Macau and Mainland China; Applications from Macau residents will be given priority; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . The selected candidate is expected to be onboard ASAP. This recruitment will remain open until the positions are filled. *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-8 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support , Job Application Post navigation Previous post Senior Clerk / Supervisor / Administrative Officer – Admissions Affairs Next post Senior Supervisor / Administrative Officer – Facility Management Office Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/08/senior-clerk-supervisor-administrative-off-admissions-affairs/": {
      "title": "Senior Clerk / Supervisor / Administrative Officer",
      "description": "Senior Clerk / Supervisor / Administrative Officer – Admissions Affairs – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Senior Clerk / Supervisor / Administrative Officer – Admissions Affairs Job Description Support the daily admissions and administrative operations of the Admissions Office, assist in the formulation and implementation of admissions plans and policies, and monitor the progress of admissions workflows across different regions; Design and produce promotional materials for admissions (e.g., admission brochures, posters, visual elements for websites) to enhance the University’s image and attract prospective students; Assist in planning and optimizing admission strategies, collaborating closely with relevant departments to ensure alignment with overall admission goals; Responsible for regular data collection on educational policy changes and admissions market trends to analyze admissions dynamics and source market information, consolidation and analysis to support admissions reporting and decision-making; Assist in reviewing applicant documents and managing admission systems, websites, and social media; Assist in organizing various admission-related events such as information session; and participate in activity planning and preparation work; Maintain close contact and cooperation with internal and external departments/ institutions. Perform other related tasks as required. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Education, Marketing, or a related field required; Master’s degree or above is preferred; At least one year of relevant work experience; Experience in admissions, brand promotion or higher education is advantageous. More experienced candidate will be considered for a higher position; Demonstrate proficiency in design software and copywriting, with the ability to independently create promotional materials; Fluent in Cantonese, Mandarin, and English; proficiency in Chinese and English writing is essential; Diligent, efficient, detail-oriented, with a strong sense of responsibility, service awareness, and team spirit; able to work under pressure; Willingness to duty travel and work off-site as required; Passion for the education industry is preferred; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-8 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post Senior Clerk / Supervisor (Promotion) – Rector’s Office Next post Faculty Administrative Staff Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/08/senior-clerk-supervisor-promotion-rectors-office/": {
      "title": "Senior Clerk / Supervisor (Promotion)",
      "description": "Senior Clerk / Supervisor (Promotion) – Rector’s Office – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Senior Clerk / Supervisor (Promotion) – Rector’s Office Job Description Assist in developing promotional plans for events or projects, utilizing social media and internal/external channels to enhance visibility and participation. Execute promotional initiatives, assist in preparing submission materials, and coordinate internal data integration. Create promotional content and produce multimedia materials (e.g., short videos, graphics, presentations). Liaise and communicate with internal university departments and external partners. Oversee the application and management of the university’s visual identity system to ensure consistency and accuracy across all promotional materials. Manage the archiving, updating, and version control of governance documents related to the Rector’s Office, ensuring compliance with current policies and regulations. Monitor the implementation of important university policies and documents across departments, regularly preparing execution reports and improvement recommendations. Assist in drafting university-level regulations, management procedures, and guidelines, conducting legality and feasibility assessments. Track post-implementation progress of policies to ensure departmental understanding and compliance. Support the Rector’s Office and other departments as needed to improve overall team efficiency. Requirement Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Public Administration, Data Analysis, Legal or a related field; Master’s degree is preferred. Minimum of 3 years of work experience; preferably in promotional planning or management. Strong planning and project management skills. Excellent analytical, organizational, and planning abilities. Proficiency in digital marketing and multimedia production. Solid document and information management skills, with familiarity in word processing and MS Office applications. Excellent organizational and time management abilities, capable of handling multiple tasks simultaneously. Detail-oriented, able to work independently, meticulous, responsible, and resilient under pressure. Team player with excellent communication skills and a proactive attitude. Fluency in Cantonese, Mandarin, and English; proficiency in Chinese and English writing; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-8 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post Laboratory Technician – Faculty of Data Science Next post Senior Clerk / Supervisor / Administrative Officer – Admissions Affairs Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/08/laboratory-technician-faculty-of-data-science/": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Laboratory Technician – Faculty of Data Science – 澳門城市大學人事處 Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Laboratory Technician – Faculty of Data Science Job Description Responsible for the daily operations, maintenance, and IoT networking configuration for faculty laboratories among campus; Participate in building of faculty network and information security system; formulate, promote, and implement information security risk management principles, processes, and standards; Plan network security for faculty laboratories, construct and operate security infrastructure, and support anti-intrusion network systems; Plan, design, adjust, and optimize the faculty network architecture and performance; Research and support curriculum development, provide hardware configuration guidance, and compile laboratory manuals; Assist in refining data security contingency plans, manage laboratory data archiving, and privacy protection processes; Complete other tasks in laboratory management and technical development as assigned by supervisor. Requirements Hold a master’s degree or above in computer science, data science, artificial intelligence, or related fields; Fluent in Chinese and English writing and communication skills; Proficient in Chinese and English computer operations, including Microsoft Office software, Python, SQL development tools, Linux operating systems, and port configuration; Mastery of Kubernetes architecture and cloud-native deployment; preference for candidates with AI Agent or knowledge base project experience; At least 3 years of relevant work experience in laboratory management or similar roles; preference for those from higher education institutions or large organizations; Preference for candidates with experience in laboratory management, project management, or curriculum development; Good work attitude, meticulous, good communicator, team player, and able to work independently; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-8 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post Project Officer – Human Resources Office Next post Senior Clerk / Supervisor (Promotion) – Rector’s Office Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處"
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/08/project-officer-human-resources-office/": {
      "title": "Project Officer",
      "description": "Project Officer – Human Resources Office – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Project Officer – Human Resources Office Job Description Provide strategic human resources advice to departments and supervisors; participate in departmental development planning and policy formulation; Conduct regular labour market research in the higher education sector, analyze salary trends, talent mobility, and policy developments, and propose forward-looking strategic recommendations; Oversee employee relations management, including staff communication, conflict mediation, and fostering overall employee relations and organizational climate within the University; Coordinate internal data analysis and report writing; develop action plans and improvement measures for HR-related issues; Assist in handling major or sensitive personnel cases, providing professional assessment and communication support; Assist in planning and preparing collaborative activities between the department and external organizations; Perform other related tasks and duties as assigned. Requirement Master’s degree or higher; preference for candidates with degrees in Statistics, Education Management, or Law-related fields; 7 years or more of relevant work experience, including at least three years in the education sector; Possess strong data consolidation, report writing, and analytical abilities; Experience in handling complaints, disciplinary matters, and labor disputes preferred; Familiar with the higher education and regional cooperation policy frameworks of Macau and Mainland China; Fluent in Chinese and English, with excellent written proficiency in both languages; knowledge of other languages is a plus; Detail-oriented, responsible, and with strong teamwork, interpersonal, and communication skills; Mature, organized, able to work independently and maintain professional judgment under pressure; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login. *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-8 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post Rector’s Secretary – Rector’s Office Next post Laboratory Technician – Faculty of Data Science Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/09/08/administrative-secretary-rectors-office/": {
      "title": "Rector’s Secretary",
      "description": "Rector’s Secretary – Rector’s Office – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Rector’s Secretary – Rector’s Office . Job Description Handle daily administrative affairs in the Rector’s Office; Responsible for the planning and arrangement of Rector’s duties and work schedule; Responsible for Organizing various meetings convened by the Rector; Communicate and coordinate between internal and external units and the Rector; Responsible for external liaison of the Rector, including visits reception and public relations; Handle enquiries and suggestions from internal and external parties, and coordinating relevant replies or meeting arrangements; Responsible for drafting important university administrative documents, meeting minutes, contract agreements, etc.; Responsible for monitoring the implementation of the university’s policies, decisions, and major work arrangements as directed by the leadership; Perform other tasks and duties as assigned. Requirement Master’s degree or above; with qualifications in Education, Public Administration, English, or related disciplines is preferred; Minimum of 5 years of work experience; preferably in higher education, government administration, and corporate management; With project management experience; Fluency in Cantonese, Mandarin, and English; proficiency in Chinese and English writing; Familiar with Microsoft Office; Strong communication and interpersonal skills; Able to work independently, be meticulous and responsible, and able to handle work pressure; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login. *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-9-8 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post CityU Hosts Seminar Exploring Strategies for Enhancing Academic Reputation from a Global Perspective Next post Project Officer – Human Resources Office Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2026/08/26/psychological-counselor-student-affairs-office-2/": {
      "title": "Psychological Counselor",
      "description": "Psychological Counselor – Student Affairs Office – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Psychological Counselor – Student Affairs Office Job Description Provide individual case counseling services to students; Regularly collect information on students’ mental health concerns and follow up accordingly; Promote mental health education initiatives and organise activities related to psychological wellbeing and counseling; Perform and support general administrative duties of the Counseling Unit; Perform other tasks and duties as assigned. Requirement Bachelor’s degree in Psychology or related disciplines, Master’s degree in Counselling, Clinical Psychology, Counselling and Psychotherapy is preferred; Minimum 3 years of relevant work experience, with experience in psychological crisis intervention and management for university students is preferred; A recognized registration as a psychotherapist or equivalent professional qualification is preferred; Possess relevant experience in organizing small groups and large-scale activities; Fluent in Cantonese, Mandarin and English, with proficiency in written Chinese and English; priority will be given to candidates who can use English as the primary working language and demonstrate strong English writing skills; Strong communication and presentation skills; Demonstrate a strong sense of responsibility, independence, maturity, proactiveness, team spirit, and a strong passion for helping others; Macau residents will be given priority consideration. Application Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2026-8-26 By tong sofia Categorized as Administrative Support Post navigation Previous post Over 80 Elite Scholars Join CityU Injecting Fresh Momentum into Teaching and Research Next post CityU Holds Seminar on Teachers’ Professional Ethics and Conduct to Explore the Core Competencies and Development Strategies for University Teachers in the New Era Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2025/10/10/head-of-quality-assurance-office-2/": {
      "title": "Head of Quality Assurance Office",
      "description": "Head of Quality Assurance Office – 澳門城市大學人事處 Our Functions News News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Head of Quality Assurance Office Job Description Overseeing and managing the following, including but not limited to: Institutional quality auditing; Programme development and validation; Programmes/modules review and modification; Quality assurance review of academic provisions (assessment moderation, annual and periodic programme review); Professional accreditation by statutory organisations; Academic governance (management, improvement and implementation of policies and procedures, regulations, codes of practices, protocols, guidelines and terms of references); Academic enhancement and educational innovation (continuous professional development and lifelong learning); Educational award/funding application; Teaching and learning seminar/colloquium; Supervision of academic offering/teaching; Student survey and services evaluations; Teaching performance award. Working actively and closely with academic units to ensure all academic setting are in compliance with the requirements of Education and Youth Development Bureau and other relevant government/statutory authorities. Other University affairs as assigned. Job Qualifications Master’s degree or above, preferably in Business Administration, Education Administration or Law; Minimum 9 years of working experience, in particular, quality assurance and standards in higher education setting and global affairs is preferred; Ability to make independent decisions with a strong sense of empowerment; Strong leadership with good interpersonal, communication and analytical skills; The post holder must be a proactive, dynamic, and self-motivated individual with good relationship building skills and high standards of professionalism; Excellent written and spoken English, Cantonese, and Mandarin with high level of technical accuracy. Application Procedures Interested applicants please register and fill out the application form via the recruitment system: https://career.cityu.edu.mo/Job/Login . Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. Published 2025-10-10 By Staff Clickr Categorized as Leader and Management Post navigation Previous post CityU Celebrates Mid-Autumn Festival with Charity Mooncake and Festive Fun Next post Gearing Up for the National Sport EventCityU Hosts Pickleball Beginner Experience Class for Staff Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處 ."
    },
    "https://hro.cityu.edu.mo/en/2025/04/01/part-time-teaching-staff/": {
      "title": "Part-time Teaching Staff",
      "description": "Part-time Teaching Staff – 澳門城市大學人事處 Menu Close Our Functions News Open menu News Training Recruitment Activity Job Application Open menu Leader and Management Teaching Administrative Support Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Search for: Search Button Part-time Teaching Staff Job Description Teaching in related fields Other tasks including course outline preparation, consultation, invigilating, marking, etc. Job Qualifications Candidate should possess a Master Degree or above Teaching experience in higher education o relevant industrial working experience is an advantage Good command of written and spoken English, Cantonese and Mandarin The vacancy is available to Macau Residents only Interested applicants may submit their CV and indicate their preferred teaching subjects/areas via the official contact details provided on each faculty’s website. For enquiries, please contact Human Resources Office at (853) 2878 7937. *Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only.* Published 2025-4-1 By Staff Clickr Categorized as Teaching Post navigation Previous post Nationwide Recruitment Fair Series – Shanghai Next post CityU Hosts the “Student Incident Crisis Intervention and Handling Skills” Seminar Contact Room A204, Administrative Building 2F, Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira Taipa, Macau. Tel: +853 2878 1698 Fax: +853 2878 8081 Email: hroinfo@cityu.mo Office Hours Monday to Friday 9:00-12:45 and 13:45-18:00 (Closed on Saturdays,Sundays and Public Holidays) Quick Links Our Functions Job Application Staff Benefits FAQs Contact Us Copyright © 2023 澳門城市大學 - 人事處"
